.\" Man page for xlsxgrep
.TH XLSXGREP 1 "August 2026" "xlsxgrep 0.0.33" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
xlsxgrep \- search text in spreadsheet format files
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B xlsxgrep
[\fIOPTION\fR]...
.I PATTERN
.I FILE
[\fIFILE\fR]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B xlsxgrep
searches for a text pattern in spreadsheet format files.
It works similarly to
.BR grep (1),
but operates on XLSX, XLS, XLSM, CSV, TSV, and ODS files.
.PP
When a match is found, output depends on the selected search mode.
In row mode (the default), matching rows are printed with fields separated by a tab.
In column mode, whole columns containing at least one match are printed vertically, one cell per line.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show help message and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Display version information and exit.
.TP
.BR \-P ", " \-\-python\-regex
Treat
.I PATTERN
as a Python regular expression.
This is the default.
.TP
.BR \-F ", " \-\-fixed\-strings
Treat
.I PATTERN
as a fixed string, not a regular expression.
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-ignore\-case
Ignore case distinctions in
.I PATTERN
and input data.
.TP
.BR \-w ", " \-\-word\-regexp
Force
.I PATTERN
to match only whole words.
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-count
Print only a count of matches per file.
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-recursive
Search directories recursively.
.TP
.BR \-H ", " \-\-with\-filename
Print the file name for each match.
.TP
.BR \-N ", " \-\-with\-sheetname
Print the sheet name for each match.
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-files\-with\-match
Print only the names of files that contain a match.
.TP
.BR \-L ", " \-\-files\-without\-match
Print only the names of files that do not contain a match.
.TP
.BI \-S " SEPARATOR"
.BI \-\-separator " SEPARATOR"
Use
.I SEPARATOR
as the field separator in row output.
The default is a tab character.
.TP
.BR \-Z ", " \-\-null
Output a zero byte (ASCII NUL) instead of the usual newline after each match.
.TP
.B \-\-row
Search rows and print matching rows.
This is the default search mode.
.TP
.B \-\-column
Search columns and print whole matching columns vertically.
.SH SEARCH MODES
.TP
.B Row mode
(\fB\-\-row\fR, default)
If any cell in a row matches
.IR PATTERN ,
the entire row is printed on one line with fields separated by the configured separator.
.TP
.B Column mode
(\fB\-\-column\fR)
If any cell in a column matches
.IR PATTERN ,
every cell in that column is printed, one per line.
.SH SUPPORTED FORMATS
csv, ods, tsv, xls, xlsx, xlsm
.SH EXAMPLES
Search a spreadsheet case-insensitively:
.PP
.RS
.nf
xlsxgrep \-i "foo" foobar.xlsx
.fi
.RE
.PP
Count matches and include file names when searching a folder recursively:
.PP
.RS
.nf
xlsxgrep \-c \-H \-r "(?i)foo|bar" /folder
.fi
.RE
.PP
Search columns and print matching columns vertically:
.PP
.RS
.nf
xlsxgrep \-\-column "error" report.xlsx
.fi
.RE
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Matches were found, or no error occurred.
.TP
.B 1
No matches were found, or a usage error occurred.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR grep (1) , pdfgrep (1)
